                    .d-flex.flex-column.flex-md-row.justify-content-between.mb-4
                        .flex-grow-1
                            h3.mb-0 Depression Tendency in Twitter Users
                            .subheading.mb-2 Natural Language Processing, Prof. Niranjan
                            p.mb-2 Built an NLP system to classify tweets as suggestive or not suggestive of depression, and extended it to estimate the depression tendency of individual Twitter users.
                            ul.mb-0
                                li Scraped ~20K tweets from public accounts using Selenium and Python scripts, added neutral/positive tweets, and reduced dataset bias through manual annotation.
                                li Preprocessed text by filtering short tweets and removing emojis, hashtags and media posts.
                                li Built a Logistic Regression baseline (scikit-learn) on TF-IDF and averaged Word2Vec (Gensim) sentence representations, with hyperparameter and solver tuning.
                                li Compared recurrent deep learning models against transformers; BiLSTM with Attention and the state-of-the-art RoBERTa model achieved 92.5% accuracy.
                                li Evaluated models on accuracy, precision, recall and F1, along with training/validation loss analysis.
                            p.mb-0.mt-2 #[a(href='https://github.com/abhiraj26/depression-tendency-twitter-nlp', target='_blank', rel='noopener') View Repository]
                        .flex-shrink-0
                            span.text-primary Sep 2020 - Dec 2020

                    .d-flex.flex-column.flex-md-row.justify-content-between.mb-4
                        .flex-grow-1
                            h3.mb-0 Do Popular Movies Endure Over Time?
                            .subheading.mb-2 Prof. Steven Skiena
                            p.mb-2 Built a machine learning model to predict the present-day popularity of movies from attributes known at the time of release, to understand why some films endure over time.
                            ul.mb-0
                                li Integrated data from IMDb, a ~5,000-movie Kaggle dataset, Google Trends, and The Movie Database API.
                                li Performed data cleaning, normalization, de-duplication and anomaly detection, and resolved entity-matching issues across sources (sequels, remakes, title variations, actors' stage names).
                                li Engineered features and built a regression baseline, then explored Random Forest, Gradient Boosting and Neural Network models with K-fold cross-validation for hyperparameter tuning.
                                li Analyzed factors behind long-term popularity and visualized trends across decades.
                            p.mb-0.mt-2 #[a(href='https://github.com/abhiraj26/movie-popularity-prediction', target='_blank', rel='noopener') View Repository]
                        .flex-shrink-0
                            span.text-primary Oct 2019 - Nov 2019

                    .d-flex.flex-column.flex-md-row.justify-content-between
                        .flex-grow-1
                            h3.mb-0 Offline Handwritten Signature Verification
                            .subheading.mb-2 Prof. Akriti Nigam
                            p.mb-2 Built a biometric verification system to distinguish genuine handwritten signatures from forgeries for fraud prevention and authentication.
                            ul.mb-0
                                li Pre-processed scanned signature images through binarization, morphological dilation/erosion, skeletonization (thinning) and pruning, then cropped each to its bounding box to isolate the strokes.
                                li Extracted directional and geometric features &mdash; aspect ratio, baseline slant, centroid, and counts of termination/trifurcate/intersection points &mdash; using a grid-based approach.
                                li Trained and compared SVM and ANN classifiers on the CEDAR signature database (55 writers, 24 genuine and 24 forged signatures each) across two train/test splits.
                                li Evaluated both models on sensitivity, specificity and accuracy from confusion-matrix analysis; SVM outperformed ANN, reaching up to ~91.7% accuracy.
                            p.mb-0.mt-2 #[a(href='https://github.com/abhiraj26/offline-signature-verification', target='_blank', rel='noopener') View Repository]
                        .flex-shrink-0
                            span.text-primary Jan 2017 - May 2017

